comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-16T09:03:59.357Z",pi-glm,"PR checks test (22)/test (26) both fail at test/exact-gates.test.ts:183 'operational entry points enforce real audits through direct CLI processes': the self-host gate reports the committed selfhost.bundle is not byte-identical to the committed source for .github/workflows/pm-github-sync.yml and pm-github-closeout.yml because the bundle still contains the old pm-github caller shape (2026.11.04 pin plus pm-github-version input). Fix: regenerate the bundle with self-host:write and commit it alongside the workflow pin. Both open review threads (Greptile on the sync caller, CodeRabbit on the closeout caller) flag exactly this and are valid."
  "2026-11-16T09:33:35.895Z",pi-glm,"Gate results at the pushed head: typecheck pass, lint pass, changelog:check pass (CHANGELOG.md already up to date, no manual edits), self-host workflow-contract gate accept:self-host pass ('the committed bundle's tip tree is byte-identical to the committed source except validated external action revisions'), node --test test/self-host.test.ts pass (69 tests). The exact-gates local run of 'operational entry points enforce real audits through direct CLI processes' hits the helper's fixed 60s child-process cap on this slow host (60.2s vs 9.7s on CI); the equivalent uncapped accept:self-host gate passes, so the earlier ETIMEDOUT is environmental. Both review threads are addressed by the regenerated committed bundle (PRRT_kwDOToJT7M63oH4X, PRRT_kwDOToJT7M63o3j2)."
  "2026-11-16T12:04:05.551Z",codex-sol,"Codex continuation: preserved and fast-forwarded the already-pushed shared-reference diagnosis commit 6df6f27; main is already included. Rechecking existing self-host fix and both original test matrix failures without treating an interrupted full test run as passing."
  "2026-11-16T12:19:27.572Z",codex-sol,"Direct job logs confirm both original failures: 132765234753 log lines 28661-28664 and 132765234957 lines 5533-5536 report removed pm-github-version lines still in the committed bundle. Existing fix commit 8f55d67 regenerated it; 6df6f27 retained and refreshed it with shared-reference diagnosis. Thread PRRT_kwDOToJT7M63oH4X is already resolved remotely; remaining PRRT_kwDOToJT7M63o3j2 has the same valid issue addressed by that bundle. No thread actions performed. Typecheck, lint, changelog and tracker validation pass. The default linked self-host test runner hit its 120-second wrapper limit under shared load; rerunning with an explicit 900-second wrapper budget, without changing test assertions or production budgets. The full npm suite is still running."
  "2026-11-16T12:55:03.338Z",codex-sol,"Verified resumed snapshot commit 15f5adc with npm run accept:self-host: committed bundle is byte-identical to committed source except validated external action revisions. Focused linked node --test test/self-host.test.ts rerun with --timeout 900 completes 63/63, 0 fail/cancel/skip/todo, in 338454 ms; the prior default-wrapper 120-second timeout is excluded from passing evidence. Typecheck, lint, changelog:check and tracker validation pass. Both original test matrix failures and review threads are addressed by the existing bundle regeneration plus this tracker-aligned snapshot. Full npm test remains active without a terminal result at receipt preparation and is not counted as passing. No PM_TEST_DEPTH tier exists on this branch. Release this claim for orchestrator review and retain the separate shared-reference diagnosis commit."
  "2026-11-16T13:21:48.118Z",codex-sol,"Bounded final receipt: the full npm test attempt did not reach terminal suite accounting after more than an hour and was stopped as a task-owned process tree within the continuation stop window. It is incomplete and excluded from passing evidence; no interrupted full run is retained as certification. The independently completed focused self-host suite remains 63/63 and the committed bundle verification passed on 1bda11b. All other recorded required narrow gates pass. Regenerate the snapshot with this final stop receipt and verify committed-source equality again; leave the item in progress and ownership released."
